From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:32:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda: layer-sliced prompt fills over a slice-aware
 AFD wire (MiaAI-Lab recipe patch 0062)

TF_GLM_FILL_BUDGET_MS > 0 runs a prompt chunk started while other streams decode a few layers at a time: each slice
sized from startup layer timings (sliced_fill.LayerCosts) to about that many ms, a decode round between two slices
(one token a stream, or drafted with TF_GLM_FILL_DRAFTS=1), the chunk's rows kept in the engine's prompt buffers and
its commit after its last layer. A request alone fills whole forwards. Off unless set: unset or 0, every prompt chunk
is one forward and the messages are the ones before.

- sliced_fill.py: the recipe's file unchanged, with the credit header.
- decode.prefill_chunk_steps, forward.compute_steps (the recipe's unsplit branch only: no hyper-connection split
  here, so split_layer_steps is not taken), multi_prefill.prefill_piece_steps.
- multi.py: the suspended chunk (FILLPART / MFILLPART ops, checked in parse), slices sized by LayerCosts, short
  rounds between slices, grouped fills, cache moves (_used counts the chunk's rows) and cancellation mid-fill (the
  server's client poll on the engine's callback), /health's sliced_fill counters; engine.py: both ranks' settings
  check and the startup line; afd_parallel_check reads the two settings before the wire opens.

The AFD wire's slice mode is this tree's own design, not part of the recipe: MODE_SLICE = 5, wire version 2 in the
settings handshake (a node of the old wire is refused at settings_mismatch). A slice is a forward over MoE positions
a .. a + n - 1 of a chunk's rows; its first request's MCDMA header has word 3 = a and word 6 = n (modes 1 and 3 and
every word they use unchanged); the expert's next_forward takes a slice's first request at its own position and
_window runs only those layers; the attention's begin(rows, chunk=True, slice=(a, n)) keeps per-slice bookkeeping,
its out-of-step refusal now also covers a slice that stopped early, and TF_AFD_CHECK keys a slice's hashes
afd_chk/{seq}/{a}+{n}/{peer}. The startup layer timings run as whole prompt-chunk forwards with the experts live.

Tests: tests/test_glm_sliced_fill.py (sliced == unsliced at world 1 over a checked wire whose header table the real
McdmaTransport.header writes, and at two ranks; grouped chunks; fp8 rings; MTP and DFlash2; a round between slices;
a move between slices, with a mutant; cancellation mid-fill; the startup timings; parse; the settings),
tests/test_glm_afd_slice_wire.py (slices round-trip over the fake MCDMA pair between eager windows, the header words,
the old wire refused both ways, a slice stopped early, malformed slice headers, the check's keys).

Credit: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md ("GLM sliced prompt fills") and the ported code's comments name MiaAI-Lab and the patch.

Co-authored-by: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
